# ==============================================================================
# 🚀 THIS IS A COPIER TEMPLATE, NOT A PROJECT
# ==============================================================================
# There is no pyproject.toml and no installable package at the root. Everything
# a generated project receives lives under template/, and comes with its own
# .gitignore.
#
# This file only keeps the template repository itself clean — plus the secrets
# section below, which is NOT optional: this repository is public, and a .env
# committed once stays in the history forever.

# ==============================================================================
# 🔐 SECURITY & SECRETS (THE MOST IMPORTANT PART)
# ==============================================================================
.env
.env.*
# The wildcard is required: Copier filters the template through .gitignore, and
# the shipped file is named `.env.sample.jinja` in the sources.
!.env.sample*
*.pem
*.key
# *.json is ignored on purpose: GCP service account keys have unpredictable
# names (my-project-1234567-abcdef.json) and a leak is expensive.
# To version a legitimate JSON file, add a targeted exception:
#   !config/settings.json
*.json

# ==============================================================================
# 🧹 LOCAL ARTIFACTS OF THE TEMPLATE REPOSITORY
# ==============================================================================
# Nothing here is shipped: `_exclude` in copier.yml is what protects a
# generated project from a local run's leftovers.
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.ruff_cache/
.pytest_cache/

data/
logs/
mlruns/
mlflow.db
mlflow.db-*
.prefect/
*.log

.DS_Store
*.Identifier
.claude/settings.local.json
